# Asset contract

The game loads every asset from `assets/` (owned and delivered by `artist`).
Paths are relative to the delivery root. Every asset is optional at load time:
if a file is missing or fails to load, the game falls back to plain drawn
shapes / silence and logs `asset missing: <path>` to the console, so a build is
always playable. The final build is expected to have all of them.

The game is drawn on a fixed logical canvas of **800 x 500 px**, scaled to the
window with nearest-neighbour (pixelated) scaling, so pixel art should be drawn
at 1x for that size.

| Path | Format | Size | Used for |
|---|---|---|---|
| `assets/img/logo.png` | PNG, transparent | up to 640 x 200 | Title screen logo, centred, top third |
| `assets/img/paddle.png` | PNG | 12 x 80 (drawn stretched to the paddle rect if different) | Both paddles (the player's is on the left) |
| `assets/img/ball.png` | PNG | 12 x 12 | Ball |
| `assets/img/centerline.png` | PNG, transparent | 4 x 24 tile (repeated vertically) | Dashed centre line |
| `assets/palette.css` | CSS | — | `:root` custom properties `--bg`, `--fg`, `--accent`, `--dim` (colours); `--font-family` (font-family stack) used for all text |
| `assets/fonts/*` | woff2/ttf | — | Declared with `@font-face` inside `palette.css`, family named in `--font-family` |
| `assets/audio/paddle.wav` | WAV | < 1 s | Ball hits a paddle |
| `assets/audio/wall.wav` | WAV | < 1 s | Ball bounces off top/bottom wall |
| `assets/audio/score.wav` | WAV | < 1 s | A point is scored |
| `assets/audio/win.wav` | WAV | < 2 s | Player wins the match |
| `assets/audio/lose.wav` | WAV | < 2 s | Computer wins the match |

Where it is loaded: `src/assets.js` (the list above is `ASSET_PATHS` there),
`index.html` (`<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/palette.css">`).

Fallback colours when `palette.css` is absent: bg `#0b0f14`, fg `#e8f0e8`,
accent `#7cff9a`, dim `#3a4a40`; font `monospace`.
